{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Mr Ellison, I've got the obs and that chemist list when you're ready.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Come through. Dr Nguyen. Umm, sorry about the wait, what's the trouble today?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Burning.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Where?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Chest.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Both sides, or just the—",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Left.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Err, when did that start?",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Sorry, can I—",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hang on a tick.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Two.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Chemist has perindapril, uh, perindopril four milligrams once a day for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): Eight.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Err, we'll sort that dose in a minute. Two days, yeah?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): And blisters?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): Few.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Shirt rub makes it worse?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Panadol, two tablets in the morning?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Chickenpox as a kid?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever, cough, or short of breath?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Eyes painful, or vision off?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Bowels alright?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Allergies to any medicine?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Anyone living with you?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Daughter's pregnant, yes?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Blood pressure today is 152 over 88 millimetres of mercury, pulse 76 beats a minute, weight 81 kilos.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): So, burning on the left chest for two days, a few blisters, worse when the shirt rubs, panadol two tablets in the morning. The perindopril I'll leave with no dose, the list says four milligrams and you said eight. That fair?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): I can see four small blisters on the left chest in a band, with redness around them, and they do not cross the midline. My working impression is shingles, herpes zoster, given that rash and chickenpox as a child. That's provisional only. No swab today.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll start you on valasyclovir, sorry, valaciclovir, one gram by mouth three times a day for seven days for the shingles, starting today. Pick it up from the chemist this arvo.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): Keep the blisters covered and don't share towels. Your daughter shouldn't touch them, and she should stay away until they crust over, seeing she's pregnant.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I can put the bloods in for Thursday morning, nurse at eight.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yes, book that. Kidney function and a full blood count Thursday morning, no fasting, just drink some water beforehand. If those are borderline we do the third test, the liver ones.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): You can take panadol two tablets up to four times a day if the pain needs it, not only mornings. I'll see you in two weeks. If it does not settle, a scan. If the blisters spread or you feel properly crook, come back sooner."
 ],
